      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Methane Phase Diagram\n\nMethane exhibits different phases (solid, liquid, gas) depending on temperature and pressure conditions:\n\n- **Critical Point**: At 190.56 K (-82.59°C) and 4.5992 MPa, there is no distinction between liquid and gas phases.\n- **Triple Point**: At 90.69 K (-182.456°C) and 0.011696 MPa, solid, liquid, and gas phases coexist in thermodynamic equilibrium.\n- **Boiling Point**: At normal pressure (1 atm), methane boils at 111.51 K (-161.6°C).\n\n## Key Properties at Standard Conditions (25°C, 1 atm)\n\n- **State**: Colorless, odorless gas\n- **Density**: 0.657 kg/m³\n- **Molecular Weight**: 16.042 g/mol\n- **Specific Gravity**: 0.554 (relative to air)\n- **Flammable**: Yes (Autoignition temp: 810 K / 537°C)\n- **Thermal Conductivity**: 0.0339 W/(m·°C)\n- **Specific Heat (Cp)**: 2.232 kJ/(kg·K)\n\n## Applications\n\nMethane is primarily used as:\n- Feedstock for chemical industry\n- Main constituent of natural gas\n- Energy source for heating and power generation"
